use { bumpA, readB } from modlib

# expect: ok
# stdout:
#   1
#   42
# Cross-file `var` reference: `a.fai` defines `bumpA` which reads
# the var `seed` declared in `b.fai`. Pre-fix, the checker resolved
# names file-by-file in alphabetical order — a function in the
# alphabetically-earlier file failed with `Unknown name` for vars in
# alphabetically-later files. After the fix, a per-module pre-pass
# declares all top-level vars/lets before any function body is
# checked, so the order doesn't matter.
def main
    @return Void
do
    print(bumpA())
    print(readB())
end
